# Pinned digests for every executable binary blob tracked in this repository.
#
# Format:  <repo-relative path>  <sha256>
#
# WHY
# ---
# Appendix F §5 records that no auditor framed the supply-chain posture as an aggregate
# delivery blocker: there is no SBOM, no dependency pinning by digest, no provenance
# attestation and no signed release artifact for any of the seven components. Current
# federal software-supply-chain expectations (EO 14028, NIST SSDF self-attestation) treat
# that as a submission blocker in its own right.
#
# `buildtools/atak-gradle-takdev.jar` is the sharpest case. It is a 148 KB binary blob that
# is tracked, redistributed, has an unstated licence, and — critically — is EXECUTED as a
# Gradle classpath dependency on every build. A substituted jar runs attacker-controlled
# code inside the pipeline that signs and publishes artifacts. It was pinned by nothing at
# all: the old workflow checked only that the file EXISTED and printed its byte count.
#
# The `atak` job in .github/workflows/ci.yml verifies the takdev jar against this file
# before invoking Gradle, and fails the build on a mismatch or on an unrecorded digest.
#
# ADDING AN ENTRY
# ---------------
# Never record a digest without first establishing where the binary came from. A pinned
# digest for a blob of unknown provenance pins the wrong thing — it guarantees you keep
# running the same unverified code. Record the provenance in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md at the
# same time.

# ── ATAK TAK-devkit Gradle plugin (executed on the build classpath) ──────────
# Provenance: shipped inside the ATAK CIV SDK. Licence UNSTATED — see
# THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, "Unresolved". Both trees carry a byte-identical copy.
ATAK5.6/buildtools/atak-gradle-takdev.jar  f430b41b03b95fad0db34bbe80a1eebf5b9965b6c4977a01995b4869dd5ff333
ATAK5.7/buildtools/atak-gradle-takdev.jar  f430b41b03b95fad0db34bbe80a1eebf5b9965b6c4977a01995b4869dd5ff333

# ── Gradle wrapper (executed by ./gradlew) ───────────────────────────────────
# Provenance: the Gradle project. Apache-2.0. Both trees carry a byte-identical copy.
# NOTE: gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties additionally carries a distributionSha256Sum
# for the Gradle distribution itself; this pin covers only the bootstrap jar.
ATAK5.6/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar  76805e32c009c0cf0dd5d206bddc9fb22ea42e84db904b764f3047de095493f3
ATAK5.7/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar  76805e32c009c0cf0dd5d206bddc9fb22ea42e84db904b764f3047de095493f3

# ── TAK devkit lint rules (loaded by the Android Lint task) ──────────────────
# Provenance: shipped inside the ATAK CIV SDK. Licence UNSTATED.
ATAK5.6/.takdev/aars/takdevlint.aar  7acc4d2cb574f09a3143d122a025340022aac1ea97edeb0f3371802de2f7aba7
ATAK5.7/.takdev/aars/takdevlint.aar  7acc4d2cb574f09a3143d122a025340022aac1ea97edeb0f3371802de2f7aba7

# ── Signing keystore (NOT executable; recorded for identification only) ──────
# This is the STOCK ATAK CIV SDK development keystore, not a project identity:
#   alias wintec_mapping, O=WinTec Arrowmaker, created 2011-05-19, serial 4dd50358,
#   SHA1withRSA, 1024-bit RSA, password `tnttnt`
# md5 de161723bca27d5da9dd16052ee18cae — byte-identical to the SDK's own android_keystore,
# which is why C-40 is adjudicated MEDIUM rather than a credential leak: the key is already
# in the hands of every ATAK plugin developer worldwide and no history rewrite is warranted.
# It is pinned here so that a substitution — the case that WOULD matter — is detectable.
ATAK5.6/app/featurelink.keystore  5a5ec442c96d117c7fa393d8402af4056a650c1a35efa419223cdac5fae30a15
ATAK5.7/app/featurelink.keystore  5a5ec442c96d117c7fa393d8402af4056a650c1a35efa419223cdac5fae30a15
